  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIBDP 2100 process dialogue</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment, financed through the Partners for Water (PfW) Program and executed by the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO), aims to foster bilateral cooperation in water and delta management between Bangladesh and the Netherlands. The main objective is to design a collaborative dialogue process to support the continuation of the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 (SIBDP2100), a strategic framework for adaptive delta management adopted by Bangladesh. This process will involve key stakeholders from both countries, focusing on knowledge sharing and innovation, while addressing recent political changes that might affect the plan&#x2019;s support. The assignment will culminate in a report outlining the process setup, stakeholder engagement, and a Terms of Reference for the dialogue facilitation.</narrative>
  </description>
